Minnesota Statutes 2024, section 144G.51, is amended to read:

144G.51 ARBITRATION.

[-(a) An assisted living facility must-]

[+ If an assisted living facility includes an arbitration provision in the assisted living contract, the provision and contract must: +]

[+(1)+] clearly and conspicuously disclose, in writing [-in an assisted living contract-], any arbitration provision in the contract that precludes[-,-][+ or+] limits[-, or delays-] the ability of a resident [+or the resident's agent +]from taking a civil action[-.-][+; +]
