Minnesota Statutes 2024, section 144G.51, is amended to read:

144G.51 ARBITRATION.

If an assisted living facility includes an arbitration provision in the assisted living contract, the provision and contract must:

(1) clearly and conspicuously disclose, in writing , any arbitration provision in the contract that precludes or limits the ability of a resident or the resident's agent from taking a civil action;
(2) adhere to Minnesota law and any other applicable federal or local law;

